<ValidationSubNav />

<h2>Root tier</h2>
<div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="fa-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Member</th><th>Signature</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr><td><code>IFaValidator&lt;TModel&gt;</code></td><td><code>void Configure(FaValidationBuilder&lt;TModel&gt; builder)</code></td><td>one implementation per model type</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>AddFaValidator&lt;TModel, TValidator&gt;()</code></td><td><code>IServiceCollection</code> extension</td><td>registers <code>TValidator</code> as <code>IFaValidator&lt;TModel&gt;</code>, scoped</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
</div>

<h2 class="fa-mt-5">FaValidationBuilder&lt;TModel&gt;</h2>
<div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="fa-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Method</th><th>Returns</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr><td><code>Field&lt;TValue&gt;(string propertyName, Func&lt;TModel, TValue&gt; accessor)</code></td><td><code>FaFieldValidationBuilder&lt;TModel, TValue&gt;</code></td><td>starts (or resumes) declaring rules for one property; <code>propertyName</code> is a plain string, pass <code>nameof(...)</code></td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>RemoveField(string propertyName)</code></td><td><code>void</code></td><td>drops every rule declared for a property so far — how a form-tier override starts a field's rules over from nothing</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
</div>

<h2 class="fa-mt-5">FaFieldValidationBuilder&lt;TModel, TValue&gt;</h2>
<p>Every method is chainable — returns the same builder, so calls stack.</p>
<div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="fa-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Method</th><th>Constraint</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr><td><code>Must(Func&lt;TValue, bool&gt; predicate, string errorMessage)</code></td><td>none</td><td>the one real primitive — any predicate; false shows <code>errorMessage</code></td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>Required(string errorMessage = "This field is required.")</code></td><td>none</td><td>non-null, and non-whitespace for strings</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>Between(TValue min, TValue max, string? message = null)</code></td><td><code>TValue : IComparable&lt;TValue&gt;</code></td><td>inclusive both ends; not for nullable value types (<code>Nullable&lt;T&gt;</code> doesn't implement <code>IComparable&lt;T&gt;</code>) — use <code>Must</code> for those</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>EqualTo(TValue expected, string? message = null)</code></td><td>none</td><td>via <code>EqualityComparer&lt;TValue&gt;.Default</code>; named <code>EqualTo</code>, not <code>Equals</code>, so it can't collide with <code>object.Equals</code></td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>MaxLength(int max, string? message = null)</code></td><td><code>TValue</code> is <code>string</code></td><td>a <code>null</code> value passes — pair with <code>Required</code> if empty shouldn't be allowed either</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
</div>

<h2 class="fa-mt-5">FaModelValidator&lt;TModel&gt;</h2>
<p>Component. Placed inside an <code>EditForm</code>, alongside (not instead of) <code>DataAnnotationsValidator</code> — both populate the same <code>ValidationMessageStore</code>.</p>
<div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="fa-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Type</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr><td><code>ConfigureValidation</code></td><td><code>Action&lt;FaValidationBuilder&lt;TModel&gt;&gt;?</code></td><td>form tier — runs after the root validator, on the same builder</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
</div>

<h2 class="fa-mt-5">FaValidationMessage&lt;TValue&gt;</h2>
<p>Component. Standalone stand-in for the stock <code>ValidationMessage&lt;TValue&gt;</code>, for a field shown with <code>ShowValidationMessage="false"</code> whose error should render somewhere other than directly under it.</p>
<div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="fa-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Type</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr><td><code>For</code></td><td><code>Expression&lt;Func&lt;TValue&gt;&gt;</code></td><td>required — field-identity extraction only, not a rule-authoring expression tree</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>CssClass</code></td><td><code>string?</code></td><td></td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
</div>

<h2 class="fa-mt-5">Each input's own validation parameters</h2>
<p><code>FaInput</code>, <code>FaSelect</code>, <code>FaTextarea</code>, <code>FaCheckbox</code> all carry these two:</p>
<div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="fa-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Type</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr><td><code>ShowValidationMessage</code></td><td><code>bool</code></td><td>defaults <code>true</code> — renders the field's own inline error automatically</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>Validate</code></td><td><code>Func&lt;TValue, string?&gt;?</code></td><td>element tier — evaluated fresh every render, always additive to the model/form tiers</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
</div>

<h2 class="fa-mt-5">FaForm&lt;TModel&gt;</h2>
<div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="fa-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Type</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr><td><code>UseFaValidation</code></td><td><code>bool</code></td><td>opts into this system alongside <code>DataAnnotationsValidator</code>; defaults <code>false</code></td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>ConfigureValidation</code></td><td><code>Action&lt;FaValidationBuilder&lt;TModel&gt;&gt;?</code></td><td>form tier; ignored unless <code>UseFaValidation</code> is set</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
</div>

<h2 class="fa-mt-5">FaDate / FaCurrency Min/Max</h2>
<p>
    <code>Min</code>/<code>Max</code> are plain component parameters, not bound model
    fields — this doesn't route through <code>IFaValidator</code> at all. Each
    component checks its own two parameters directly and renders the same
    <code>.fa-validation-message</code> look when <code>Max</code> ends up before
    <code>Min</code>. Shown, not thrown — a transient bad combination doesn't crash
    the render tree.
</p>

<h2 class="fa-mt-5">CSS classes</h2>
<div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="fa-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Class</th><th>Applied to</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr><td><code>.fa-input-invalid</code> / <code>.fa-select-invalid</code></td><td>the input/select box itself, when it has any validation messages</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>.fa-validation-message</code></td><td>the inline error text under a field</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
</div>
<p>Both use <code>var(--fa-ember)</code>, this library's existing danger/error color token.</p>
